afe for people to work  here they also gave us photos of a  damaged turbine the reality is with  coastal sort of not generating any  energy hundreds of thousands of people  will be without power what's the reality  do you think people are gonna have to  sort of get used to having power maybe  half  and not having it the other half we're  going to walk 24 hours around the clock  I hear you and a lot of people are happy  to hear that but be as realistic with me  as possible or less than a month compare  that to what the head of Puerto Rico's  Electric Power Authority says Jose Ortiz  the CEO if I faith it would be out for  probably over a year how much of this is  earthquake related or how much is it  just old equipment that hasn't been  cared for and updated it's both really  you know to be honest those plans were  have over 60 years basically imagine you  have a taxi 60 years old and you are  required to run that 24/7 said you know  it's that's the kind of business we're  running when folks here in Puerto Rico  heard Jose Ortiz say it could take a  year to get coastal soil back up and  running  there was a trending hashtag on Twitter  Jose Ortiz renunciant for him to resign  listen this is what he told me he said  they're asking FEMA to bring in a 500  megawatt generator to go ahead and get  this place back up and running when FEMA  heard him say that in our interview Gail  they reached out to me and said we have  not agreed to do that and we cannot do  that under the current emergency  declaration that Puerto Rico is  operating under they need a major  disaster declaration and as of now the  governor has not requested it and the  president has not signed it Wow David  first Bravo to you very interesting  information that you have and you're  literally standing outside and asked to  come in and they say okay come in that's  amazing they did and again this morning  they came back to us and said come back  in we want to show you some more so we  wanted the people here